# Test execution integrity: a skipped suite is never a pass

Restaurant integration suites under `tests/integration/**` wrap in
`describe.skipIf(!authEnvReady)` (see `tests/integration/helpers/env.ts`).
When local Supabase env is missing, the suite **skips and reports green**.
That is not a pass.

## Why suites silently skip

`authEnvReady` requires the public Supabase URL/anon key plus
`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`. Absent keys → skip, 0 failures. Connection
errors (`ECONNREFUSED`, `ENOTFOUND`) MUST fail the run when
`RESTAURANT_INTEGRATION_STRICT=true` — never convert an unreachable
Postgres into a skip.

## The integration command (always fail-closed)

```powershell
$env:RESTAURANT_INTEGRATION_STRICT = 'true'; pnpm test:integration <path>
```

A skipped `describe.skipIf(!authEnvReady)` suite is never green.

## Preflight: confirm the target actually executed

A clean-looking result is not enough — check the reporter summary:
- PowerShell: `pnpm test:unit <path> 2>&1 | Select-String -Pattern "skipped|passed|failed"`.
- The target must appear in the **failed** count (Red) or **passed** count
  (Green/Refactor) — not `skipped`, and not `0 tests collected`.
- If it skipped or collected 0 tests, you are **infra-blocked**.

## Shared BLOCKED (infra) report shape

```
## <Red|Green|Refactor> — BLOCKED (infra)
<phase-specific line>
Command: <the exact command run>
Observed: <skipped count / "0 tests collected">
Remedy: <e.g. `npx supabase start; npx supabase db reset --local`, then re-run>
Note: returning to orchestrator — a skipped suite cannot validate this criterion.
```

## The doctrine

**A skipped suite is never a RED, never a GREEN, never a clean
re-verification — it is BLOCKED.** This applies to the phase agents,
`/commit` re-running the gates, and `/sdd-to-tdd` orchestrating the loop.
